Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:04:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Freeciv45 edges: the sidebar's wheel and right-click extras
 and its indicators

With gui_qt_freeciv45_edges on the sidebar is hidden, and its extras went
with it. They now sit on the matching right-edge buttons, each with a
tooltip line:

- Cities: the wheel goes up through the other nations' cities, down
  through your own.
- Nations: the wheel goes up through the other nations' capitals, down to
  your capital; a right-click opens the current diplomacy meeting (an
  observer gets the observe menu).
- Units: the wheel goes up through the other nations' units, down as W
  does; a right-click centres on the focus unit.
- Research: a right-click offers the advances to research now.

The wheel first returns to the map and closes the city overlay, so it works
from a report too. A notch is 120; a touchpad's smaller steps add up to one.
The same functions as the sidebar's run, unchanged. The sidebar's fallback
right-click (back to the map from any other button) is not carried over:
the Map button does it.

The four indicators (research progress, global warming, nuclear winter,
government) sit in the top strip left of the year and turn, drawn at the
strip's icon height, with the game summary as their tooltip. A click or a
right-click offers the government menu, as a right-click on the sidebar's
indicators did. set_indicator_icons redraws them with the sidebar's.

panels.md sections 8.1 and 8.2, issue 146.
